# Pin line endings to LF in the working tree as well as in the index.
#
# Without this, core.autocrlf=true (the default on this Windows machine) wants
# CRLF in the working tree while Biome's formatter writes LF. Git then reports
# every formatted file as modified even though the committed bytes are
# identical -- 80 files at once after the first `biome check --write`, with an
# empty `git diff`, which is alarming and completely spurious. Pinning LF makes
# the formatter and git agree, and matches CI, which runs on Linux.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: never touch these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
